- How would you extend to non-Horn clauses?
- How would you handle incremental updates when facts change?

## Why This Is Asked

Temporal-like constraints on feature flags across release cycles test three-valued propagation and branching heuristics—skills essential for configuration validation at scale.

## Key Concepts

- Kleene three-valued logic with implication defined as ¬A ∨ B
- Propagation rules for ¬, ∨, ∧, and →
- Backtracking search treating U as a first-class domain value

## Code Example

```javascript
// Three-valued backtracking propagator sketch
const VALUES = { T: 2, U: 1, F: 0 };
const NOT = { T: 'F', F: 'T', U: 'U' };
const OR = (a, b) => VALUES[a] >= VALUES[b] ? a : b;
const AND = (a, b) => VALUES[a] <= VALUES[b] ? a : b;
const IMPLIES = (a, b) => OR(NOT[a], b);

function propagate(constraints, assignment) {
  let changed = true;
  while (changed) {
    changed = false;
    for (const [ante, conseq] of constraints) {
      const a = assignment[ante], c = assignment[conseq];
      if (a === 'F' && c !== 'F') { assignment[conseq] = 'F'; changed = true; }
      if (a === 'T' && c !== 'T') { assignment[conseq] = 'T'; changed = true; }
      if (c === 'F' && a !== 'F') { assignment[ante] = 'F'; changed = true; }
    }
  }
  return assignment;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How does the branching heuristic affect worst-case complexity?
- How would you extend this to N time steps?

Why This Is Asked
Assess the ability to reason with Kleene 3-valued semantics in a constrained CSP and to design a propagation/backtracking approach that handles unknowns.

Key Concepts
- Kleene 3-valued logic: T>U>F; ¬T=F, ¬F=T, ¬U=U; ∧/∨ use min/max under T>U>F; A→B := ¬A ∨ B.
- Constraint propagation in a small CSP with unknowns; existence of a model containing U.
- Backtracking strategies to prune non-viable branches.

Code Example
```javascript
const V = {T:'T', F:'F', U:'U'}
functionNot(x){ if (x==='T') return 'F'; if (x==='F') return 'T'; return 'U' }
function kleeneOr(a,b){ if (a==='T' || b==='T') return 'T'; if (a==='U' || b==='U') return 'U'; return 'F' }
function kleeneAnd(a,b){ if (a==='F' || b==='F') return 'F'; if (a==='U' || b==='U') return 'U'; return 'T' }
function implies(a,b){ return kleeneOr(functionNot(a), b) }
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to apply paraconsistent LP semantics to CSP-style constraint solving, including constructing a concrete model and a propagation strategy.

## Key Concepts

- Priest's Logic of Paradox (LP)
- Paraconsistent 3-valued truth tables for ∨, ∧, ¬, →
- CSP backtracking with forward checking under LP
- Concrete satisfying assignment with at least one B

## Code Example

```javascript
// LP semantics for 3-valued logic (T > F, B = both)
function lpNot(v){ return v=== 'T' ? 'F' : v==='F' ? 'T' : 'B';}
function lpOr(a,b){ if(a==='T' || b==='T') return 'T'; if(a==='B' || b==='B') return 'B'; return 'F';}
function lpAnd(a,b){ if(a==='F' || b==='F') return 'F'; if(a==='T' && b==='T') return 'T'; return 'B';}
function lpImp(a,b){ // a -> b = (¬a) ∨ b
  return lpOr(lpNot(a), b);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to detect unsatisfiable constraint sets efficiently in LP?
- How would you scale this to hundreds of variables with incremental propagation?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical logical deduction and simple SAT handling in a controlled, small-domain setting.

## Key Concepts
- Implication with negation
- Disjunction
- Satisfiability search
- Backtracking basics
- Early termination on first valid assignment

## Code Example
```javascript
function isSat(A,B) {
  // Clause1: (!A => B)  == (A || B)
  // Clause2: (B => A)   == (!B || A)
  // Clause3: (A || B)
  return (A || B) && (!B || A) && (A || B);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend to three variables with similar clauses?
- How does short-circuit evaluation affect performance in larger clause sets?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical structuring of 3-valued reasoning via propagation on a single formula.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene 3-valued semantics: T>U>F; ¬ swaps T/F, U→U; ∨/∧ use max/min.
- Expression-level propagation and branch pruning.
- Backtracking search with partial assignments.

## Code Example
```javascript
function eval3(a,b,c){
  const not=(v)=> v==='T'? 'F' : v==='F'? 'T' : 'U';
  const or=(x,y)=> {
    const rank={'F':0,'U':1,'T':2};
    return rank[x] >= rank[y] ? x : y;
  };
  const and=(x,y)=> {
    const rank={'F':0,'U':1,'T':2};
    return rank[x] <= rank[y] ? x : y;
  };
  return and(or(a,b), or(not(c), a));
}
```

